			<div class="content" id="post-content-3913576">
									

<p>I think expecting the reader to &quot;figure out the trick&quot; of using lvl5 or using a hex reader is a step too far, in all honesty.</p>
<p>Ultimately, it's a question of how far you want the reader to make the effort necessary to receive your story, though. With the note on the author's post, it's not too hard, and I appreciate that. I would never have used a hex reader (nor would I feel happy with a skip that specifically requires one).</p>
<p>I do, however, appreciate the <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OGsv0pJemTY" target="_blank">Prince of Darkness</a> vibe of the message, and despite the message itself being something I could expect, I still enjoyed the story overall. +1.</p>
<p>(Also for anyone who hasn't seen Prince of Darkness, it's incredible SCP fuel. It's definitely one the main inspirations for my work I've had over the years, and it's been almost 30 years since I've seen it in total.)</p>

